      <h2>1. Why Real-Time Video Chat Is Different</h2>

      <p>Video communication combines several channels at once: spoken words, tone of voice, facial expressions, gestures and timing. This makes it different from text-based communication, where most of the interaction is represented through written language.</p>

      <h3>1.1 More Information Than Text Alone</h3>

      <p>Text messages can be efficient, but they do not always communicate tone clearly. A short sentence can sometimes be interpreted differently depending on how the reader imagines it was said.</p>

      <p>Voice adds information through pronunciation, tone and pauses. Video adds another layer through visible cues.</p>

      <h3>1.2 Video Does Not Eliminate Misunderstandings</h3>

      <p>More information does not automatically mean perfect understanding. Facial expressions can be ambiguous, internet connections can interrupt conversations, and people can still interpret the same words differently.</p>

      <p>Video should therefore be viewed as an additional communication channel rather than a guarantee of better communication.</p>

